                 <h1>The Sibling Primitive: Programmable Claims</h1>
 
-                <p>Institutions exist to issue, govern, and adjudicate <strong>claims</strong>. A claim is a future cash flow with a probability distribution over its timing and amount. The unifying lens of finance is that the value of any asset is the probability-weighted discounted future cash flow it represents. Equity is a claim on residual earnings. Debt is a claim on principal and coupon at scheduled times. Sukuk is a claim on Sharia-permissible asset usage. Parametric insurance is a contingent claim on adverse-event cash flow. Tokenised real-world assets are claims on off-chain cash flow. Sports prediction, parimutuel pools, and other event-contingent contracts are contingent claims on outcome cash. Options, futures, and swaps are claims constructed from claims.</p>
